{
  "id": "u10-l06",
  "unit": "u10-culture",
  "title": "Invitations & guests",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "Bengali invitations use the **future** as a gentle request: **আমাদের বাসায় আসবেন** — literally 'You will come to our home', meaning 'Please do come!' Formally: **আপনাকে দাওয়াত দিলাম** 'I'm inviting you'.\n\nA **মেহমান** (guest) is treated with great honour: expect tea, sweets and **পিঠা**, and to be asked **খাবেন?** more than once. Saying **না** once is often taken as politeness; accept a little.\n\n**জন্য** 'for' follows a genitive: **এই উপহার আপনার জন্য** 'This gift is for you'. Wishes: **শুভ জন্মদিন** 'Happy birthday', **ঈদের শুভেচ্ছা** 'Eid greetings'.\n\n**Kolkata:** নেমন্তন্ন (invitation), অতিথি (guest).",
